<description>
Clean a noisy regular array by reconstructing its repeated rectangular sprite and erasing everything outside the slots.

Input structure
- The background is the most common color.
- Non-background cells form a regular grid of solid rectangular sprite slots, plus sparse stray foreground noise.
- Every slot contains a corrupted copy of the same sprite, preserving non-background occupancy.

Rule
- Find the dense row bands and dense column bands of the slot array.
- For each relative position inside the sprite rectangle, take the unique majority color across all slots.
- Fill every slot with that recovered sprite and set all other cells to background.

Key insight
- The intended sprite support is the Cartesian product of dense row bands and dense column bands; noise is too sparse to enter the high-density bands consistently.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "regular array of equal-size solid rectangular sprite slots plus sparse foreground noise outside the array; each slot is a corrupted copy of the same sprite",
  "transform": "recover the sprite by unique per-coordinate majority across slots; replace every slot with the recovered sprite and clear all cells outside the slot array to background"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 21-24 rows x 22 cols; background is 0
  slot_array:
    layout: 3 rows x 2-3 cols of identical rectangular slots
    slot_size: 4-6 rows x 4-6 cols (uniform within a grid)
    row_gap: 1-2 (uniform); col_gap: 1-2 (uniform)
    top_margin: 1 [observed]; left_margin: 1-2
    bottom_margin: 3-5; right_margin: 4-6
    total_slots: 6-9 (>=4 required by solver)
  sprite:
    fully non-bg (no background cells in sprite)
    distinct_non_bg_colors: 3-4
    color_regions: rectangular or irregular blocks; no specific symmetry required
  noise:
    outside_slots: 26-32 scattered non-bg pixels on bg cells using sprite colors
    within_slots: 7-9% of slot cells corrupted to a different sprite color (not bg)
    constraint: per-pixel majority vote across all slots must recover the true sprite,
      so no position can have >49% of slots corrupted to the same wrong color

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick slot_rows=3, slot_cols=2-3, slot_h=4-6, slot_w=4-6, row_gap=1-2, col_gap=1-2
    2. Build the sprite (slot_h x slot_w) with 3-4 non-bg colors, no bg cells
    3. Place slots in a regular grid with top_margin=1, left_margin=1-2, gaps as chosen;
       add bottom_margin=3-5 and right_margin=4-6 to set total grid size
    4. Fill every slot with the sprite to form the output
    5. Corrupt ~8% of cells within each slot by changing to a different sprite color;
       ensure no position has majority corrupted (at most floor(n_slots/2)-1 slots wrong)
    6. Scatter 26-32 noise pixels on bg cells outside slots using sprite colors
```
